WEBVTT

00:00:02.940 --> 00:00:06.520
Onii-chan! Drink my soup all up, okay?

00:00:06.850 --> 00:00:10.250
Make it delicious! Make it delicious!

00:00:12.780 --> 00:00:14.910
Here. Your roasted stone lizard.

00:00:15.220 --> 00:00:19.020
A-And it's not like I made this 
especially for you or anything, got it?

00:00:19.020 --> 00:00:22.490
But we don't want anything left over, 
so make sure you eat it all, okay?

00:00:22.490 --> 00:00:23.040
Yes, ma'am!

00:00:24.710 --> 00:00:26.250
Ladies, enjoy.

00:00:26.590 --> 00:00:28.770
It's hot, so please be careful.

00:00:28.770 --> 00:00:30.090
We will!

00:00:31.680 --> 00:00:35.470
Did you enjoy your meals, everyone?

00:00:35.470 --> 00:00:36.460
Yes!

00:00:36.460 --> 00:00:38.550
Here is your bill.

00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:45.810
One, two, three, four...

00:00:46.140 --> 00:00:48.090
Everyone worked so hard today!

00:00:48.090 --> 00:00:50.250
There were tons of customers.

00:00:50.250 --> 00:00:52.320
It's exhausting.

00:00:52.320 --> 00:00:53.600
I feel the same.

00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:54.770
We did it!

00:00:55.530 --> 00:00:59.080
Today's sales beat our previous record high!

00:00:59.340 --> 00:01:00.330
Really?

00:01:00.500 --> 00:01:02.850
But we will not be satisfied with this!

00:01:02.850 --> 00:01:05.320
Tomorrow, we'll do our best to sell even more!

00:01:05.320 --> 00:01:06.460
Let's do it!

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:08.250
<i>Stare...</i>

00:01:08.250 --> 00:01:09.820
What? What is it?

00:01:09.820 --> 00:01:11.690
Are you unhappy about something?

00:01:11.690 --> 00:01:14.640
Unhappy? You ask that after making 
us do those embarrassing—

00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:15.970
Don't say it, Reina-san!

00:01:16.340 --> 00:01:19.000
Our contract with her says we can stay here

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:21.600
for a reduced rate in exchange 
for serving customers.

00:01:21.880 --> 00:01:24.940
If we defy her now, it will 
only increase our rent.

00:01:26.500 --> 00:01:28.150
It's nothing.

00:01:28.150 --> 00:01:29.640
I see.

00:01:29.640 --> 00:01:32.360
In that case, I'll be counting 
on all of you tomorrow, too!

00:01:36.840 --> 00:01:37.610
<i>I win.</i>

00:01:38.090 --> 00:01:39.370
<i>I lost.</i>

00:01:42.160 --> 00:01:43.900
We need to earn some money.

00:01:43.900 --> 00:01:45.140
Yes, we do.

00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:50.210
A high-paying quest...

00:01:50.210 --> 00:01:51.400
A high-paying quest!

00:01:51.400 --> 00:01:52.060
A high-paying...

00:01:52.060 --> 00:01:53.000
...quest!

00:01:54.550 --> 00:01:57.410
There! Wyvern hunting!

00:03:25.890 --> 00:03:28.020
Didn't I Say to Make My Abilities 
Average in the Next Life?!

00:03:28.970 --> 00:03:33.020
<b>Episode 9</b>

00:03:28.970 --> 00:03:33.020
<b>Didn't I Say Wyvern Hunting?!</b>

00:03:37.710 --> 00:03:39.680
The wyvern hunt! We'll do it!

00:03:39.680 --> 00:03:41.850
It would be better not to.

00:03:41.850 --> 00:03:42.570
Huh?

00:03:42.960 --> 00:03:45.260
You're turning us away before we've even tried?

00:03:45.260 --> 00:03:47.200
You're saying we can't beat it?

00:03:47.420 --> 00:03:50.830
Not at all. I don't think it will be 
an issue, in terms of fighting ability.

00:03:51.350 --> 00:03:57.460
The Crimson Vow has three mages, 
all of whom can use powerful attack magic.

00:03:57.730 --> 00:04:01.900
I'm sure that you would be able to 
deal damage even to a flying wyvern.

00:04:02.480 --> 00:04:03.550
Gyaass!

00:04:03.800 --> 00:04:05.220
In that case, it'll be easy!

00:04:05.220 --> 00:04:07.570
We'll get 30 gold pieces.

00:04:07.570 --> 00:04:09.240
The thing is, it runs away.

00:04:09.240 --> 00:04:09.970
Huh?

00:04:10.530 --> 00:04:15.100
After suffering a certain amount of damage,
 wyverns retreat to their dens.

00:04:16.440 --> 00:04:17.680
That's cowardly!

00:04:17.680 --> 00:04:21.180
They are wild animals, so outside 
of extreme circumstances,

00:04:21.180 --> 00:04:23.150
they won't fight to the death.

00:04:23.510 --> 00:04:25.310
But if they run, all we 
have to do is chase them...

00:04:25.310 --> 00:04:27.650
Unless you can fly through 
the sky, it's not possible.

00:04:28.600 --> 00:04:32.810
Additionally, a wyvern's territory is 
said to be tens of kilometers wide,

00:04:32.810 --> 00:04:35.040
so finding its den is impossible.

00:04:36.530 --> 00:04:38.880
And this is the real problem...

00:04:38.880 --> 00:04:39.600
Huh?

00:04:39.600 --> 00:04:41.130
There's more?

00:04:41.720 --> 00:04:44.760
Wyverns can remember people's faces.

00:04:44.760 --> 00:04:45.760
What?

00:04:46.060 --> 00:04:49.100
If it's fought someone and gotten beat up,

00:04:49.100 --> 00:04:51.330
it won't go near that person again.

00:04:52.460 --> 00:04:53.390
But that means...

00:04:53.770 --> 00:04:56.900
You mean we only have one 
chance when fighting a wyvern?

00:04:57.250 --> 00:04:58.620
Exactly.

00:04:58.620 --> 00:04:59.960
What?

00:04:59.960 --> 00:05:04.050
In the past, many Hunters have gathered 
the best equipment money can buy

00:05:04.050 --> 00:05:06.110
and attempted this quest.

00:05:06.550 --> 00:05:09.400
But not a single one succeeded.

00:05:09.400 --> 00:05:11.960
All they received were 
wounds from their battle,

00:05:11.960 --> 00:05:15.130
huge bills, and the quest's 
penalty for breach of contract.

00:05:16.920 --> 00:05:20.840
In short, the only ones who try this 
quest are idiots, rookies, or heroes.

00:05:23.760 --> 00:05:24.960
Then we'll take it!

00:05:24.960 --> 00:05:27.010
Wha? Did you hear what I just said?

00:05:27.010 --> 00:05:28.010
Of course!

00:05:28.200 --> 00:05:30.950
Thirty gold pieces is too juicy to pass up!

00:05:30.950 --> 00:05:34.480
A wyvern may be only a subspecies, 
but it is a dragon-type monster.

00:05:34.480 --> 00:05:37.350
If we beat it, we can call 
ourselves dragon slayers!

00:05:37.350 --> 00:05:38.810
What we're saying is that we're...

00:05:39.150 --> 00:05:42.940
idiots, rookies, and heroes.

00:05:42.940 --> 00:05:44.240
Hey! Reina-san!

00:05:44.240 --> 00:05:47.890
Did you just point at me 
when you said "idiots"?

00:05:47.890 --> 00:05:49.290
No.

00:05:49.290 --> 00:05:50.920
Are you sure?

00:05:50.920 --> 00:05:52.100
I understand.

00:05:52.100 --> 00:05:55.040
We'll leave the wyvern hunting quest to you.

00:05:56.620 --> 00:05:57.380
However...

00:05:57.380 --> 00:05:59.560
Please, be very careful.

00:05:59.560 --> 00:06:00.340
We will!

00:06:07.280 --> 00:06:09.180
You girls are the Hunters?

00:06:09.460 --> 00:06:11.160
Yes! We are...

00:06:11.160 --> 00:06:12.450
Hunters from the royal capital...

00:06:12.450 --> 00:06:13.520
The Crimson Vow!

00:06:13.520 --> 00:06:14.320
At your service!

00:06:14.950 --> 00:06:15.770
I'm requesting a change.

00:06:15.770 --> 00:06:16.890
Why?

00:06:17.280 --> 00:06:19.290
It's too much for you girls.

00:06:19.290 --> 00:06:22.170
Go ahead and collect some of the medicinal 
herbs around here and head back.

00:06:22.170 --> 00:06:25.120
We came to hunt the wyvern.

00:06:25.120 --> 00:06:27.530
Here's the receipt for the quest!

00:06:29.180 --> 00:06:30.950
Looks like you're serious about this...

00:06:34.150 --> 00:06:36.400
The thing showed up about two months ago.

00:06:36.400 --> 00:06:40.670
It's made the forest its territory, 
and about once every ten days,

00:06:40.880 --> 00:06:42.830
it steals livestock from the village.

00:06:44.720 --> 00:06:46.280
And it's not just Hunters.

00:06:46.280 --> 00:06:49.090
The local lord attempted to subdue it, too.

00:06:49.430 --> 00:06:52.100
None of his men were able to defeat it.

00:06:53.320 --> 00:06:56.960
So how are you girls planning to fight it?

00:06:57.470 --> 00:06:58.860
Leave it to us!

00:06:58.860 --> 00:07:00.730
We have a secret plan!

00:07:04.240 --> 00:07:09.580
He really is a good village head, 
giving us a cow to lure the wyvern here.

00:07:09.580 --> 00:07:13.300
Isn't it just because having it learn what 
humans taste like would cause more problems?

00:07:13.300 --> 00:07:14.870
That seems plausible.

00:07:15.330 --> 00:07:18.060
But I feel sorry for the poor cow
 who's going to get eaten.

00:07:18.060 --> 00:07:20.500
Little cow, we'll protect you, okay?

00:07:26.830 --> 00:07:29.620
It's all right. There, there.

00:07:30.410 --> 00:07:31.920
Even the cow...

00:07:31.920 --> 00:07:33.540
Oh! Looks like it's here!

00:07:37.810 --> 00:07:39.140
Gyaass!

00:07:39.570 --> 00:07:40.740
The time has come.

00:07:40.740 --> 00:07:43.480
Huh? Does that wyvern look 
like it's got something?

00:07:43.480 --> 00:07:46.520
A calf, maybe? Do you think it's 
already attacked another village?

00:07:46.970 --> 00:07:49.650
If that's true, it might not come this way.

00:07:49.820 --> 00:07:50.990
Gyaass!

00:07:50.990 --> 00:07:53.280
It's not a calf, it's a log, isn't it?

00:07:56.240 --> 00:07:57.560
Run!

00:08:01.720 --> 00:08:04.560
A bombing run? That wyvern's good.

00:08:04.560 --> 00:08:08.960
But if it thinks we're the same as the other 
groups that came hunting it, it'll regret it!

00:08:09.520 --> 00:08:13.180
But it's completely out of range 
of a magic attack. What do we do?

00:08:13.670 --> 00:08:15.900
If it won't reach, we just
 have to make it reach.

00:08:16.390 --> 00:08:18.930
Reina-san! Start casting!

00:08:18.930 --> 00:08:21.240
That means you've got 
something in mind, right?

00:08:21.240 --> 00:08:22.570
All right. I'm counting on you.

00:08:22.570 --> 00:08:23.140
You've got it!

00:08:24.140 --> 00:08:26.800
Blaze brightly, righteous fires of Hell!

00:08:28.480 --> 00:08:29.480
Huh?

00:08:29.480 --> 00:08:30.570
Here we go!

00:08:30.570 --> 00:08:33.560
Thunderbird 1, go! Swing-by!

00:08:33.560 --> 00:08:34.450
Huh? Huh? Huh?

00:08:34.450 --> 00:08:35.770
Huh? Huh? Huh? Huh?

00:08:37.700 --> 00:08:40.740
Take this magical Reina Gun!

00:08:44.030 --> 00:08:46.830
Reina-san! You're supposed to attack!

00:08:49.710 --> 00:08:50.550
Huh?

00:08:53.060 --> 00:08:54.360
Updraft!

00:08:54.360 --> 00:08:55.630
Help Reina-san land safely.

00:09:08.630 --> 00:09:10.500
Unit 1 seems to have failed.

00:09:10.500 --> 00:09:10.980
Huh?

00:09:11.580 --> 00:09:14.490
Now then, Unit 2, Pauline-san. Shall we?

00:09:15.910 --> 00:09:18.490
This move will be called 
"Pauline the Shredder"!

00:09:25.760 --> 00:09:28.520
M-Mile! I'll be Unit 2!

00:09:28.520 --> 00:09:29.810
Mavis...

00:09:29.810 --> 00:09:31.900
I'll race through the skies 
and cut down a dragon!

00:09:31.900 --> 00:09:34.210
There couldn't be a battle 
more exciting than this!

00:09:34.210 --> 00:09:35.470
Please, let me do it!

00:09:35.870 --> 00:09:37.180
All right.

00:09:37.520 --> 00:09:39.660
Mavis, I'm so sorry...

00:09:39.660 --> 00:09:40.450
It's nothing.

00:09:42.590 --> 00:09:44.620
Here we go, Mavis-san.

00:09:44.620 --> 00:09:45.820
I'm ready whenever!

00:09:46.970 --> 00:09:49.670
Thunderbird 2, go! Ready to launch!

00:09:49.670 --> 00:09:52.110
Equipped: one weapon, sword!

00:09:53.000 --> 00:09:55.070
Swing-by!

00:09:56.980 --> 00:09:59.360
Mavis Cutter!

00:10:00.080 --> 00:10:01.330
Sky Sword!

00:10:04.680 --> 00:10:05.620
No good.

00:10:07.210 --> 00:10:08.670
A draw?

00:10:09.120 --> 00:10:10.790
I still have a long ways to go...

00:10:13.840 --> 00:10:14.630
Updraft!

00:10:22.690 --> 00:10:25.100
We have to strike faster, with more accuracy.

00:10:25.920 --> 00:10:27.620
Unit 3, Pauline-san!

00:10:27.620 --> 00:10:28.310
Huh?

00:10:28.760 --> 00:10:30.000
Pauline-san?

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:31.770
Pauline-san?

00:10:32.020 --> 00:10:35.070
It's time for Pauline the Shredder!

00:10:35.070 --> 00:10:35.730
Oh!

00:10:36.080 --> 00:10:37.260
Reina!

00:10:37.260 --> 00:10:38.380
Don't come any closer!

00:10:39.310 --> 00:10:41.410
Stay back! I'm begging you!

00:10:42.080 --> 00:10:45.220
Bathing magic and laundry magic?

00:10:46.330 --> 00:10:50.780
It's because the wyvern was 
all wyverny with the wyvern's...

00:10:55.020 --> 00:10:56.990
I'll heat up some more hot water.

00:10:58.480 --> 00:10:59.540
Thank you.

00:11:01.450 --> 00:11:05.600
Honestly, that Mile! If she's gonna do 
something like that, she should tell us first!

00:11:05.910 --> 00:11:07.620
Th-That's true...

00:11:07.620 --> 00:11:09.680
Mile! You...

00:11:09.680 --> 00:11:11.000
The enemy's right above us!

00:11:11.000 --> 00:11:11.440
Huh?

00:11:14.340 --> 00:11:14.980
Take that!

00:11:15.270 --> 00:11:16.770
Please! Hit it!

00:11:18.130 --> 00:11:19.260
Yes!

00:11:21.730 --> 00:11:25.360
That hurts, Reina-san! 
Are you angry or something?

00:11:25.360 --> 00:11:29.740
Of course I am! What the heck was 
that Thunderbird or whatever?

00:11:29.740 --> 00:11:31.970
It was a revolutionary anti-aircraft
 tactic designed to

00:11:31.970 --> 00:11:34.080
quickly increase the range
 of a magical attack—Ow!

00:11:34.080 --> 00:11:37.440
Ow! Ow! I said that hurts!

00:11:37.440 --> 00:11:40.670
If we don't do something like that, 
our magic won't reach it, right?

00:11:41.120 --> 00:11:44.970
We have the chance to hunt a wyvern!
 I don't want to fail!

00:11:44.970 --> 00:11:46.000
Mile-chan!

00:11:55.660 --> 00:11:59.720
Hey, Pauline! You were thinking 
something weird just now, weren't you?

00:11:59.720 --> 00:12:01.500
Those eyes... They tell me everything.

00:12:01.500 --> 00:12:02.070
Huh?

00:12:02.400 --> 00:12:04.570
Let's go, Thunderbird 3!

00:12:04.940 --> 00:12:05.820
Okay!

00:12:06.440 --> 00:12:07.800
Gyaass!

00:12:09.750 --> 00:12:11.290
Gyaass!

00:12:11.730 --> 00:12:13.160
You're really doing this?

00:12:13.160 --> 00:12:14.020
Yes.

00:12:14.020 --> 00:12:15.790
Here we go, Pauline-san.

00:12:15.790 --> 00:12:16.910
Whenever you're ready.

00:12:16.910 --> 00:12:19.590
Thunderbird 3, ready to launch!

00:12:20.000 --> 00:12:22.850
Up until now, I've been taking into 
account the range of a sword or spell,

00:12:22.850 --> 00:12:25.220
and throwing slightly off target.

00:12:25.560 --> 00:12:28.960
But I'm not going easy on it anymore. 
I'm aiming straight for its body!

00:12:28.960 --> 00:12:29.770
What?

00:12:31.040 --> 00:12:33.020
Thunderbirds are go!

00:12:33.020 --> 00:12:34.730
Flying Pauline!

00:12:36.940 --> 00:12:38.860
Now, Pauline-san! Your magic!

00:12:39.420 --> 00:12:40.400
Something's not right!

00:12:41.990 --> 00:12:43.320
I think she passed out!

00:12:43.640 --> 00:12:45.240
Oh no! Lattice Energy Barrier!

00:12:49.080 --> 00:12:49.580
Gyaass!

00:12:54.710 --> 00:12:55.670
Gyaass!

00:12:55.670 --> 00:12:57.800
Boss! There's a wyvern falling from the sky!

00:12:57.800 --> 00:12:59.410
Who're you calling "boss"?

00:12:59.410 --> 00:13:01.560
Forget that. Just hurry up and save Pauline!

00:13:01.560 --> 00:13:02.630
You got it, boss!

00:13:02.810 --> 00:13:03.840
Updraft!

00:13:09.150 --> 00:13:11.560
Pauline-san! You did it!

00:13:13.120 --> 00:13:15.640
It seems it can't fly yet 
because of the damage.

00:13:16.160 --> 00:13:18.740
A wyvern that can't fly is just a wyvern!

00:13:18.740 --> 00:13:20.640
It's a wyvern either way then!

00:13:20.640 --> 00:13:22.360
Oh, you're right, boss!

00:13:22.360 --> 00:13:24.240
Stop calling me "boss"!

00:13:24.490 --> 00:13:26.370
Now, let's deal the finishing blow.

00:13:26.370 --> 00:13:27.200
Yeah!

00:13:27.810 --> 00:13:29.380
Gyaass!

00:13:33.880 --> 00:13:35.180
Kyaa!

00:13:36.400 --> 00:13:38.750
Kyaa!

00:13:42.640 --> 00:13:44.340
Is this a kamikaze spell?

00:13:44.780 --> 00:13:45.920
Then I will take it on!

00:13:49.370 --> 00:13:50.050
Huh?

00:13:50.320 --> 00:13:52.470
Oh no!

00:13:52.960 --> 00:13:55.970
And it's mastered the Stomach Rumble, too!
 It's really something else.

00:13:55.970 --> 00:13:57.390
Enough of that already!

00:13:58.080 --> 00:13:59.560
Now we're up.

00:13:59.890 --> 00:14:01.780
My turn. Draw!

00:14:03.020 --> 00:14:05.240
Carbon Nanotube Net!

00:14:05.240 --> 00:14:06.110
Gyaass!

00:14:07.880 --> 00:14:09.680
Karbo... What?

00:14:09.680 --> 00:14:11.360
Carbon Nanotube.

00:14:11.360 --> 00:14:14.910
I thought this might happen, so I made 
it in advance. It's a super-strong net.

00:14:18.160 --> 00:14:20.070
Now it's time for the climax.

00:14:20.070 --> 00:14:22.840
You gave us quite a bit of trouble.

00:14:22.840 --> 00:14:25.680
We can't let a single scale go to waste.

00:14:25.680 --> 00:14:30.800
This is where it starts. 
The legend of us as dragon slayers!

00:14:30.800 --> 00:14:32.930
Prepare yourself!

00:14:33.200 --> 00:14:34.100
Wait, please!

00:14:34.340 --> 00:14:35.140
Huh?

00:14:35.140 --> 00:14:37.640
Please don't kill this wyvern.

00:14:37.640 --> 00:14:38.560
What?

00:14:45.540 --> 00:14:47.170
Don't!

00:14:48.340 --> 00:14:50.390
So, who are you?

00:14:50.390 --> 00:14:54.700
I am Booneclift, the man who 
was once this wyvern's master.

00:14:54.900 --> 00:14:55.880
Huh?

00:14:55.880 --> 00:14:57.440
Master?

00:14:57.440 --> 00:14:58.830
What do you mean?

00:14:59.200 --> 00:15:01.920
It was back when I was a boy...

00:15:02.630 --> 00:15:06.550
One day, I found an injured lizard.

00:15:08.460 --> 00:15:11.820
And as I was renowned for my kindness, I...

00:15:11.820 --> 00:15:12.970
Should you say that about yourself?

00:15:12.970 --> 00:15:15.560
Also, there's no way it
looked like a normal lizard.

00:15:15.860 --> 00:15:19.270
I just couldn't abandon that lizard.

00:15:23.860 --> 00:15:26.900
I think we can already 
tell how this will end...

00:15:27.280 --> 00:15:31.990
I decided to take care of it, 
just until it healed, but...

00:15:31.990 --> 00:15:34.870
It's already clear where this is going.

00:15:36.670 --> 00:15:40.760
What I had taken in was no 
ordinary lizard! It was a wyvern!

00:15:40.760 --> 00:15:41.790
See? I knew it!

00:15:42.050 --> 00:15:45.590
But by that time, we'd already grown close.

00:15:45.790 --> 00:15:49.710
He was like a brother to me.

00:15:50.080 --> 00:15:53.000
But my parents wouldn't allow me to keep him.

00:15:53.000 --> 00:15:54.540
Of course they wouldn't!

00:15:54.540 --> 00:15:58.010
So we had to say goodbye.

00:15:58.310 --> 00:16:01.150
Saying goodbye to... the wyvern.

00:16:08.010 --> 00:16:10.490
Farewell! Live a good life!

00:16:12.700 --> 00:16:14.860
Farewell! Farewell!

00:16:23.730 --> 00:16:29.210
I cried, as I knew I would, and filled with 
unbearable feelings, I left that place.

00:16:29.720 --> 00:16:31.760
What are you two doing?

00:16:32.360 --> 00:16:34.760
So this wyvern, Rascal is...

00:16:34.940 --> 00:16:38.050
He's called Lobreth. 
Don't just go giving him names.

00:16:38.050 --> 00:16:40.180
Then, that Gyaos bird is...

00:16:40.180 --> 00:16:42.560
It's Lobreth! And he isn't a bird.

00:16:42.790 --> 00:16:44.440
Then that Ropross is...

00:16:44.440 --> 00:16:45.650
It's Lobreth!

00:16:48.720 --> 00:16:49.490
Rop—!

00:16:49.490 --> 00:16:50.160
Lob—!

00:16:50.160 --> 00:16:51.010
—ross!

00:16:51.010 --> 00:16:51.610
—reth!

00:16:54.380 --> 00:16:54.960
Rop!

00:16:54.960 --> 00:16:55.410
Lob!

00:16:55.410 --> 00:16:55.960
—ross!

00:16:55.960 --> 00:16:56.480
—reth!

00:16:56.480 --> 00:16:57.240
Ropross!

00:16:57.240 --> 00:16:57.970
Lobreth!

00:16:57.970 --> 00:16:58.200
Rop—

00:16:58.200 --> 00:16:59.860
Stop it already!

00:16:59.860 --> 00:17:01.710
And you! Stop letting an idiot's 
provocations get to you!

00:17:01.710 --> 00:17:03.540
His name doesn't matter!

00:17:03.880 --> 00:17:07.870
Given the situation,
his name's gotta be Rascal,

00:17:07.870 --> 00:17:09.840
and it screams "gyaa," 
so it's like Gyaos, but...

00:17:09.840 --> 00:17:13.300
He keeps using the name "Lobreth,"
 which doesn't capture any of it, so I...

00:17:13.570 --> 00:17:16.410
Is this the mouth? The mouth 
that just won't stop arguing?

00:17:16.410 --> 00:17:18.260
I'm really sorry, boss.

00:17:18.510 --> 00:17:22.580
At a glance, that wyvern does 
seem to be attached to you,

00:17:22.580 --> 00:17:25.610
but what proof do you have 
that it's actually your pet?

00:17:25.610 --> 00:17:28.770
We came here after receiving an 
official request from the Guild.

00:17:28.770 --> 00:17:29.740
That's right.

00:17:29.740 --> 00:17:32.480
We don't treat one wyvern any 
differently than another.

00:17:32.740 --> 00:17:35.820
If that's the case, I can prove it. Watch.

00:17:36.740 --> 00:17:39.750
O ether, tremble and quake at my will...

00:17:39.750 --> 00:17:41.240
Sonic Breath!

00:17:43.950 --> 00:17:45.550
The Stomach Rumble skill!

00:17:45.550 --> 00:17:49.110
It's Sonic Breath! Don't just 
give it whatever name you want!

00:17:49.110 --> 00:17:52.680
What is wrong with this girl? 
You need to keep her in check, boss.

00:17:52.680 --> 00:17:54.130
I'm not the boss!

00:17:54.400 --> 00:17:57.470
This magic is an original spell of mine.

00:17:57.470 --> 00:17:59.590
The only ones who can use 
it are me and Lobreth.

00:17:59.910 --> 00:18:02.440
It does seem to be true.

00:18:02.440 --> 00:18:05.560
Aw, man. And we went to all 
the trouble of catching it.

00:18:05.860 --> 00:18:08.200
I know I've done something unpardonable.

00:18:08.200 --> 00:18:10.520
And, after all that's passed, I realize 
I'm only serving my own needs.

00:18:11.140 --> 00:18:14.530
Still, I want to be with you.

00:18:14.530 --> 00:18:17.010
Won't you come back, Ropross?

00:18:19.040 --> 00:18:21.330
Oh! Lobreth! Lobreth.

00:18:21.330 --> 00:18:24.450
You said it so many times, 
you made me say it wrong!

00:18:24.780 --> 00:18:27.870
From now on, your nickname 
will be Baffled II!

00:18:27.870 --> 00:18:30.300
What kind of nickname is that?
 Don't call me that!

00:18:31.800 --> 00:18:32.790
Lobreth...

00:18:34.760 --> 00:18:38.410
Though I tossed you aside, 
you will forgive me?

00:18:38.410 --> 00:18:39.460
Thank you.

00:18:40.530 --> 00:18:43.250
Starting now, we'll always be together!

00:18:43.820 --> 00:18:45.520
We'll always be together!

00:18:46.400 --> 00:18:48.370
What a beautiful story.

00:18:48.370 --> 00:18:51.190
I have this feeling the moment's 
pretty much been ruined because of you.

00:18:54.520 --> 00:18:57.540
Looks like it isn't 
"happily ever after" quite yet.

00:18:59.200 --> 00:19:01.080
We understand the situation.

00:19:01.080 --> 00:19:04.550
But our village has suffered 
losses which are not insignificant.

00:19:04.550 --> 00:19:08.000
We can't simply agree to this.

00:19:08.320 --> 00:19:09.960
I'll make sure you're taken care of.

00:19:13.460 --> 00:19:15.440
Allow me to express my
 heartfelt congratulations

00:19:15.440 --> 00:19:17.920
at your reunion with your long-lost friend.

00:19:18.300 --> 00:19:22.050
And I promise you as well, I will 
not leave you with a loss from this.

00:19:22.520 --> 00:19:26.010
Um... Booneclift-san, who are you exactly?

00:19:26.390 --> 00:19:28.560
Me? I am...

00:19:30.850 --> 00:19:34.480
Who'd have imagined that 
Booneclift-san was a royal mage?

00:19:34.480 --> 00:19:37.000
He said he wanted to keep 
a wyvern for a pet,

00:19:37.000 --> 00:19:40.320
so I thought he had to be someone important,
 but it was still a surprise!

00:19:40.810 --> 00:19:44.250
And since he reported to the Guild 
that we'd captured the wyvern,

00:19:44.250 --> 00:19:45.760
the quest counts as completed.

00:19:45.760 --> 00:19:48.240
With this, we're officially 
dragon slayers, right?

00:19:48.540 --> 00:19:51.480
Since we also developed a 
relationship with a royal mage,

00:19:51.480 --> 00:19:54.710
this quest was an unmitigated success!

00:19:56.730 --> 00:19:59.550
Now, about the use of this money...

00:19:59.960 --> 00:20:02.220
Shall we proceed along the 
lines of our initial plan?

00:20:02.570 --> 00:20:03.600
Of course!

00:20:03.600 --> 00:20:05.680
That's why we worked so hard, right?

00:20:05.680 --> 00:20:07.850
The time has come to 
fulfill our dearest wish!

00:20:08.170 --> 00:20:10.220
In that case, we'll start our plan now!

00:20:10.220 --> 00:20:11.430
Yeah!

00:20:11.680 --> 00:20:14.100
What? You're leaving our inn?

00:20:14.310 --> 00:20:15.100
Yup!

00:20:15.440 --> 00:20:17.270
B-B-B-B-But why?

00:20:17.570 --> 00:20:19.360
My! You mean you don't know?

00:20:19.360 --> 00:20:26.510
In order to reduce our rent, we've helped
 bring in customers and serve them,

00:20:26.510 --> 00:20:28.860
but we no longer have the need to do that.

00:20:28.860 --> 00:20:32.620
After all, we're Hunters, 
not restaurant servers.

00:20:32.790 --> 00:20:35.960
Th-Th-Then you could just stay 
here at the regular rate!

00:20:36.250 --> 00:20:37.940
Huh? We can do that?

00:20:37.940 --> 00:20:39.480
That would be all right.

00:20:39.480 --> 00:20:43.040
No, it's not! The "regular rate" 
is what everyone gets charged!

00:20:43.040 --> 00:20:43.750
Huh?

00:20:43.750 --> 00:20:44.430
Tch...

00:20:44.810 --> 00:20:48.970
We were actually talking about 
moving somewhere that had a bath.

00:20:49.270 --> 00:20:50.350
A bath?

00:20:50.840 --> 00:20:52.740
There isn't one here, right?

00:20:54.320 --> 00:20:55.140
<i>We win.</i>

00:20:55.500 --> 00:20:57.230
<i>I lost.</i>

00:20:57.540 --> 00:21:01.050
That's why we wanted to discuss 
something with you, Lenny-chan.

00:21:01.050 --> 00:21:03.240
Discuss... something?

00:21:05.360 --> 00:21:09.660
Mile, this bath you built 
has a very unusual design.

00:21:10.520 --> 00:21:12.490
I've never seen the 
mountain in this painting.

00:21:12.490 --> 00:21:13.870
What mountain is it?

00:21:13.870 --> 00:21:16.330
Keroron

00:21:13.870 --> 00:21:16.330
The writing in here... What country is it from?

00:21:16.530 --> 00:21:18.540
Huh? Uh, well... It's...

00:21:18.800 --> 00:21:20.380
A secret family technique?

00:21:20.380 --> 00:21:21.840
Yes, yes, yes, yes, yes...

00:21:21.840 --> 00:21:25.990
Well, our savings have decreased, 
but I'm glad we built this.

00:21:25.990 --> 00:21:27.070
That's true.

00:21:27.070 --> 00:21:30.310
Having a bath after completing 
a quest is the best!

00:21:30.520 --> 00:21:32.560
It really is...

00:21:32.560 --> 00:21:33.480
Excuse me!

00:21:34.400 --> 00:21:37.360
Is it really okay for me to join you?

00:21:37.360 --> 00:21:39.030
Of course it is, Lenny-chan!

00:21:39.030 --> 00:21:41.710
A ten-year-old kid's got 
no reason to hold back.

00:21:41.710 --> 00:21:43.110
All right!

00:21:47.520 --> 00:21:48.740
What?

00:21:49.280 --> 00:21:52.290
Apparently, the etiquette is 
to use the buckets there

00:21:52.290 --> 00:21:54.100
to pour hot water over 
yourself before getting in.

00:21:54.100 --> 00:21:55.710
Oh, I see.

00:21:56.030 --> 00:21:59.200
Oh, this feels amazing. Baths really are nice.

00:21:59.200 --> 00:22:01.200
We can make hot water with magic,

00:22:01.200 --> 00:22:04.120
so when we're here, 
you can have a bath any time.

00:22:04.120 --> 00:22:06.880
Really? Yay!

00:22:07.420 --> 00:22:09.970
<i>We lost!</i>

00:22:09.970 --> 00:22:12.850
Didn't I Say to Make My Abilities 
Average in the Next Life?!
